# Static, not DHCP: QEMU's user-mode network is fixed (guest 10.0.2.15, gateway 10.0.2.2, DNS
# 10.0.2.3), and an address is kernel state that a mass kill cannot take away. udhcpc, killed by
# the same sysrq that /etc/inittab explains, releases its lease on the way out and leaves eth0
# with no address at all — a guest that is up and unreachable.
auto lo
iface lo inet loopback

auto eth0
iface eth0 inet static
    address 10.0.2.15/24
    gateway 10.0.2.2
